# Home directory safety .gitignore
#
# /home/lzrk IS the working tree of the PUBLIC repo savagedamage/android-security-wizard.
# Everything in this home directory that is not the corpus would leak on `git add -A`
# (.bash_history, .claude/.codex/.config/.ssh, .hermes infra incl. auth.json/state.db,
# work folders, evidence dirs). Strategy: IGNORE EVERYTHING, then whitelist only the
# corpus paths this repo tracks. New research notes live elsewhere and are backed up;
# they are deliberately NOT part of this public repo.
#
# If you add a tracked corpus file that does not match the whitelist below, add its
# negation here FIRST, then `git add` it explicitly. Never remove the `/*` baseline.

# Ignore everything at the repo root (including dotfiles)
/*

# ...except the repo's own guard and corpus files
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/android-*.md
!/shizuku-*.md
!/adb-shizuku-primer.md

# .hermes contains Hermes infra (auth.json, .env, state.db, logs, sessions, kanban,
# profiles, cron) — never publish. Only the mirrored corpus skill is part of this repo.
!/.hermes/
/.hermes/*
!/.hermes/skills/
/.hermes/skills/*
!/.hermes/skills/android-security-wizard/
